	(text "Clamp: 57.50 V on, 56.50 V off (VOH 11.7 V, 19.1M hysteresis). Spread 56.82-58.19 V full temperature, 56.99-58.02 V 0-60 C. 10 Ohm 50 W clad external: 330 W, 5.75 A.\nFET, 2 mOhm shunt (INA228 SHUNT_CAL 2000, ADCRANGE 0), 30 A Schottky and M4 terminals are sized for the leg stage 2 Ohm resistor, 29 A, 1.7 kW short time: only the\nexternal resistor swaps.\nINA228 0x4D: clamp power and energy on its own accumulator. Budget about 5 mA, 0.23 W in the LDO.\nFailure: stuck-on 330 W caught by brake NTC and opening the E-stop banks. SMDJ58A stays off under 64.4 V, spike protection only.\nRegen decision (coordinator 11-06): 10 Ohm in rev A. 30 A regen against 5.75 A clamp: BMS opening mid-brake rises 13.5 V/ms, drives stop at 60 V in about 185 us, torque drops. Leg stage fits 2 Ohm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
